"408":{"stem":"For a particular car, the linear function \\(f\\) gives the predicted power, in brake horsepower \\((\\text{bhp})\\), for engine speeds between \\(1{,}000\\text{ revolutions per minute }(\\text{rpm})\\) and \\(6{,}000\\text{ rpm}\\). According to this function, the car's predicted power is \\(433\\text{ bhp}\\) at an engine speed of \\(3{,}331\\text{ rpm}\\) and \\(600\\text{ bhp}\\) at an engine speed of \\(4{,}500\\text{ rpm}\\). The equation \\(f(x)=\\frac{1}{7}(x-a)+433\\) defines \\(f\\), where \\(x\\) is the engine speed, \\(\\text{in rpm}\\), and \\(a\\) is a constant. What is the value of \\(a\\)?"},
"409":{"stem":"\\[ 5G+45R=380 \\]\n\nAt a school fair, students can win colored tokens that are worth a different number of points depending on the color. One student won \\(G\\) green tokens and \\(R\\) red tokens worth a total of \\(380\\) points. The given equation represents this situation. How many more points is a red token worth than a green token?"},
"410":{"stem":"In a set of four consecutive odd integers, where the integers are ordered from least to greatest, the first integer is represented by \\(x\\). The product of \\(12\\) and the fourth odd integer is at most \\(26\\) less than the sum of the first and third odd integers. Which inequality represents this situation?","choices":["\\(12(x+6)\\le x+(x+4)-26\\)","\\(12(x+6)\\ge 26-(x+(x+4))\\)","\\(12(x+4)\\le x+(x+3)-26\\)","\\(12(x+4)\\ge 26-(x+(x+3))\\)"]},
"411":{"stem":"A student council group is selling school posters for a fundraiser. They use the function \\(p(x)=5x-220\\) to determine their profit \\(p(x)\\), in dollars, for selling \\(x\\) school posters. In order to earn a profit of \\(\\$900\\), how many school posters must they sell?"},
"412":{"stem":"\\[ \\begin{aligned} 4x-3y&=5 \\\\ x&=8 \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nWhat is the solution \\((x, y)\\) to the given system of equations?","choices":["\\((8, 9)\\)","\\((8, -24)\\)","\\((8, -9)\\)","\\((8, 24)\\)"]},
"413":{"stem":"Argon is placed inside a container with a constant volume. The graph shows the estimated pressure \\(y\\), in \\(\\text{pounds per square inch (psi)}\\), of the argon when its temperature is \\(x\\) kelvins.\n\n[[fig1]]\n\nWhat is the estimated pressure of the argon, in \\(\\text{psi}\\), when the temperature is 600 kelvins?","choices":["6","12","300","600"],"figs":[{"src":"math_fig/413_f1.jpg","alt":"Line graph of Pressure (psi), y, from 0 to 36, versus Temperature (kelvins), x, from 0 to 800. A line rises from about (100, 2) to about (800, 16), passing through (600, 12)."}]},
"414":{"stem":"The length, \\(y\\), of a white whale was \\(162\\text{ centimeters }(\\text{cm})\\) when it was born and increased an average of \\(4.8\\text{ cm}\\) per month for the first \\(12\\) months after it was born. Which equation best represents this situation, where \\(x\\) is the number of months after the whale was born and \\(y\\) is the length, in \\(\\text{cm}\\), of the whale?","choices":["\\(y=162x\\)","\\(y=162x+162\\)","\\(y=4.8x+4.8\\)","\\(y=4.8x+162\\)"]},
"415":{"stem":"[[fig1]]\n\nThe shaded region shown represents the solutions to which inequality?","choices":["\\(y\\ge \\frac{2}{3}x-6\\)","\\(y\\ge \\frac{2}{3}x+6\\)","\\(y\\ge \\frac{2}{3}x-9\\)","\\(y\\ge \\frac{2}{3}x+9\\)"],"figs":[{"src":"math_fig/415_f1.jpg","alt":"Graph in the xy-plane of a solid line passing through (0, -6) and (9, 0), with the region above the line shaded."}]},
"416":{"stem":"\\[ 2x+9y=7 \\]\n\nThe given equation is one equation in a system of two linear equations. If the system of equations has at least one solution, which of the following equations could be the other equation in the system?\n\nI. \\(3x+13.5y=10.5\\)\n\nII. \\(3x-13.5y=10.5\\)","choices":["I only","II only","I and II","Neither I nor II"]},
"417":{"stem":"Which system of linear equations has no solution?","choices":["\\[ -2x+3y=-9 \\]\n\n\\[ 2x-3y=9 \\]","\\[ 2x-3y=9 \\]\n\n\\[ 3x+4y=10 \\]","\\[ 2x-3y=9 \\]\n\n\\[ -6x+9y=-27 \\]","\\[ -2x+3y=9 \\]\n\n\\[ 4x-6y=18 \\]"]},
"418":{"stem":"Store A sells raspberries for \\(\\$5.50\\) per pint and blackberries for \\(\\$3.00\\) per pint. Store B sells raspberries for \\(\\$6.50\\) per pint and blackberries for \\(\\$8.00\\) per pint. A certain purchase of raspberries and blackberries would cost \\(\\$37.00\\) at Store A or \\(\\$66.00\\) at Store B. How many pints of blackberries are in this purchase?","choices":["\\(4\\)","\\(5\\)","\\(8\\)","\\(12\\)"]},
