"437":{"stem":"Kaylani used fabric measuring \\(5\\) yards in length to make each suit for a men's choir. The relationship between the number of suits that Kaylani made, \\(x\\), and the total length of fabric that she purchased \\(y\\), in yards, is represented by the equation \\(y - 5x = 6\\). What is the best interpretation of \\(6\\) in this context?","choices":["Kaylani made \\(6\\) suits.","Kaylani purchased a total of \\(6\\) yards of fabric.","Kaylani used a total of \\(6\\) yards of fabric to make the suits.","Kaylani purchased \\(6\\) yards more fabric than she used to make the suits."]},
"438":{"stem":"For a camping trip a group bought \\(x\\) one-liter bottles of water and \\(y\\) three-liter bottles of water, for a total of \\(240\\) liters of water. Which equation represents this situation?","choices":["\\(x + 3y = 240\\)","\\(x + y = 240\\)","\\(3x + 3y = 240\\)","\\(3x + y = 240\\)"]},
"439":{"stem":"[[fig1]]\n\nTo earn money for college, Avery works two part-time jobs: A and B. She earns $10 per hour working at job A and $20 per hour working at job B. In one week, Avery earned a total of s dollars for working at the two part-time jobs. The graph above represents all possible combinations of numbers of hours Avery could have worked at the two jobs to earn s dollars. What is the value of s ?","choices":["128","160","200","320"],"figs":[{"src":"math_fig/439_f1.jpg","alt":"Line segment graph with Number of hours at job A on the horizontal axis (0 to 20) and Number of hours at job B on the vertical axis (0 to 10). The segment goes from (0, 8) to (16, 0)."}]},
"440":{"stem":"\\[ \\begin{aligned} -x - wy &= -337 \\\\ 2x - wy &= 47 \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nIn the given system of equations, \\(w\\) is a constant. In the \\(xy\\)-plane, the graphs of these equations intersect at the point \\((q, 19)\\), where \\(q\\) is a constant. What is the value of \\(w\\)?"},
"441":{"stem":"For a \\(3\\)-week period in a town in Illinois, the lowest recorded temperature was \\(31\\) degrees Fahrenheit \\((^\\circ\\text{F})\\) and the highest recorded temperature was \\(67^\\circ\\text{F}\\). Which inequality is true for any recorded temperature \\(t\\), in \\(^\\circ\\text{F}\\), in this town for this \\(3\\)-week period?","choices":["\\(t \\ge 98\\)","\\(t \\ge 67\\)","\\(31 \\le t \\le 67\\)","\\(t \\le 31\\)"]},
"443":{"stem":"\\[ y = 18 - 5x \\]\n\nThe equation above represents the speed y, in feet per second, of Sheila's bicycle x seconds after she applied the brakes at the end of a ride. If the equation is graphed in the \\(xy\\)-plane, which of the following is the best interpretation of the \\(x\\)-coordinate of the line's \\(x\\)-intercept in the context of the problem?","choices":["The speed of Sheila's bicycle, in feet per second, before Sheila applied the brakes","The number of feet per second the speed of Sheila's bicycle decreased each second after Sheila applied the brakes","The number of seconds it took from the time Sheila began applying the brakes until the bicycle came to a complete stop","The number of feet Sheila's bicycle traveled from the time she began applying the brakes until the bicycle came to a complete stop"]},
"444":{"stem":"To repair a refrigerator, a technician charges $\\(60\\) per hour for labor plus $\\(120\\) for parts. Which function \\(f\\) represents the total amount, in dollars, the technician will charge for this job if it takes \\(x\\) hours?","choices":["\\(f(x) = x + 120\\)","\\(f(x) = 60x\\)","\\(f(x) = 60x + 120\\)","\\(f(x) = 60x - 120\\)"]},
