"1078":{"stem":"A function \\(p\\) estimates that there were \\(2{,}000\\) animals in a population in \\(1998\\). Each year from \\(1998\\) to \\(2010\\), the function estimates that the number of animals in this population increased by \\(3\\%\\) of the number of animals in the population the previous year. Which equation defines this function, where \\(p(x)\\) is the estimated number of animals in the population \\(x\\) years after \\(1998\\)?","choices":["\\(p(x)=2{,}000(3)^{x}\\)","\\(p(x)=2{,}000(1.97)^{x}\\)","\\(p(x)=2{,}000(1.03)^{x}\\)","\\(p(x)=2{,}000(0.97)^{x}\\)"]},
