"1487":{"stem":"[[fig1]]\n\nIn the figure shown, points \\(Q\\), \\(R\\), \\(S\\), and \\(T\\) lie on line segment \\(PV\\), and line segment \\(RU\\) intersects line segment \\(SX\\) at point \\(W\\). The measure of \\(\\angle SQX\\) is \\(48^\\circ\\), the measure of \\(\\angle SXQ\\) is \\(86^\\circ\\), the measure of \\(\\angle SWU\\) is \\(85^\\circ\\), and the measure of \\(\\angle VTU\\) is \\(162^\\circ\\). What is the measure, in degrees, of \\(\\angle TUR\\)?","figs":[{"src":"math_fig/1487_f1.jpg","alt":"Horizontal line segment PV with points P, Q, R, S, T, V from left to right. Segments QX and SX form triangle QXS below the line; segments RU and TU form triangle RUT below the line, with U lowest. Segment RU crosses segment SX at point W. Note: Figure not drawn to scale."}]},
